    <string name="tips_help"> &lt;body&gt; &lt;h1&gt;&lt;u&gt;Tips for stitching better panoramas&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/h1&gt; The following guidelines will help you make the best possible panoramas with Bimostitch. &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; &amp;#8226; Photos that are plain or clear in the area of overlap will fail to stitch.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;\n       &amp;#8226; Non overlapping photos will be automatically ignored. Ensure you capture images with not less than 25% overlap for better results.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;\n       &amp;#8226; Avoid capturing plain clear photos.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;\n       &amp;#8226; Avoid too many repeated or very similar looking structures in overlapping photos, this can lead to false matches.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;\n       &amp;#8226; Use your favorite camera app to capture overlapping images.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;\n       &amp;#8226; Make sure there is enough overlap area between photos.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;\n       &amp;#8226; Make sure to hold your phone firmly in landscape or portrait mode and rotate it such that the rotation axis passes through the camera lens. Rotate the camera in any direction but keep the camera lens on the same point as much as possible. Do not use your body as a rotation axis.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;\n       &amp;#8226; Use the camera lens as the reference point and not your body when capturing photos for stitching. Keep the lens or device at the same point as much as possible but rotate it in any direction to capture overlapping photos.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;\n       &amp;#8226; Keep the lens or camera still when snapping to avoid motion blur.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;\n       &amp;#8226; To help capture good overlapping shots keep track of the center of the previous shot and snap another when it reaches the edge.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;\n       &amp;#8226; Avoid capturing photos in direct sunlight.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;\n       &amp;#8226; Don’t merge photos with severe differences in lighting conditions.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;\n       &amp;#8226; Avoid moving objects in the area of overlap.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt; &lt;/body&gt; </string>
